.TH man 1 "26 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME 
	mmc - mkdir, mv things there, cd there
.SH SYNOPSIS
	mmc source[s] destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	makes the destination directory. then moves the files there. then cds to that directory. if dest already exists it's just mvcd.
.SH OPTIONS
	mv default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose\n\n
	mkdir default options do not work because mkdir only uses the last argument
.SH EXAMPLES
	mmc *.csv csvs
	mmc sdifji.py ../../ijsdif
.SH BUGS
	probably none
